# 孫子 (Sun Tzu) — the six insight categories and Dave's engine

## Answer
Place each section by its recorded `Source:` kind, and reach six by splitting the two largest kinds with one written question each — `instruction` into **brief** and **handoff**, `check` into **check-noisy** and **check-blind**, leaving **engine-output** (tool) and **environment** (config) whole. Pick related sections with **(c) both**: the main agent names the categories in the question, and Dave also reads the one-line index and pulls any section whose check matches, then cites `<file>#<id>`. Run Dave and Dario on **Claude Sonnet 5.5** (1M window, no price step, cache reads at 5%) as the default, revisit when the per-question load crosses 100k tokens or the whole file passes gpt-6.1-sol's 922k input cap. If the experiment's aim is set on the harness's own engine, swap to deepseek-flash and accept the unmeasured long-context quality.

